I wrote two tasks and an issue-responses file, and committed them as 8724c45c. session_plan/ is gitignored, so the git add session_plan/ from the instructions added nothing and the || true hid that. I force-added the three files with git add -f instead.

Task 01: `social.sh` spend reader (#944, evolve). This bug shows up in a real run. Run 36463335955 finished successfully but printed no_terminal_emit, meaning "the process died before reporting its usage". The script searches the log for the ↳ usage line, but yoyo switches to quiet mode when its output goes through a pipe, so that line is never printed there. daily_diary.sh already avoids this by reading the "type":"usage" record from this run's new lines in .yoyo/audit.jsonl. The task:
• Rewrite `report_social_spend to read the audit file the same way. It must report every usage record, because social.sh` can start yoyo more than once per run.
• Commit that change before running any cargo command.
• Add test cases to tests/harness_logic.sh, pulling the real function out of social.sh the way existing checks already do. The main case matches what production produces: a log with no ↳ line and a usage record in the audit file.
• Break the fix on purpose and restore it in one command, to confirm the new test catches the old behaviour.

Task 02: `--print` losing a partial answer when the stream fails (product). This comes from a fix in the Claude Code changelog. Since --print now writes only the final answer to stdout, a turn whose stream dies partway through might write nothing, even though some text already arrived. I haven't verified that it happens. The task tests first:
• It adds a local stub server that sends some text, then an error, and answers every retry the same way.
• It runs yoyo exactly as the existing --print test does and records stdout, the exit code, stderr and the number of requests.
• If the partial text already reaches stdout, the task ends with that recorded as a regression test.
• Otherwise it changes src/prompt.rs so the partial text goes to stdout with a non-zero exit code, and updates docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md. JSON output mode is out of scope and will be noted as not covered.

